Here are my timing results on a Sun ultrasparc 2/2200 in double precision.

  routine                 Mflops
                    no opt     optimized (-O)

 x*x scalar         6.629541     64.191444
 x*x vector         4.424184     22.368158
 x**2 scala         7.637088     16.617260
 x**2 vecto         5.365106     23.890512
 x**2. scal         7.654577     16.549056
 x**2. vect         5.342769     23.796837
 x**2.01 sc         1.897283      2.610437
 x**2.01 ve         0.567783      0.654413
 x*x*x scal         5.668141     32.354875
 x*x*x vect         3.702529     21.510906
 x**3 scala         4.628581     13.199857
 x**3 vecto         3.874324     21.533822
 x**3. scal         1.659949      2.512280
 x**3. vect         0.569286      0.670852
 x**3.01 sc         1.884676      2.692186
 x**3.01 ve         0.571896      0.647438

The entire code is rather long, but each pair of subroutines (scalar and
vector code) are similar to the following:


         subroutine pwr21(aa,nloop,
        $ times)
   ccccc
   ccccc  a = a*a
   ccccc
         implicit double precision (a-h,o-z)
         times = cputim()
         do 10 i = 1,nloop
           aa = aa*aa
      10 continue
         times = cputim() - times
         return
         end

         subroutine pwr22(a,b,ncycle,maxnpt,
        $ times)
   ccccc
   ccccc  b(i) = a(i)*a(i)
   ccccc
         implicit double precision (a-h,o-z)
         dimension a(*),b(*)
         sum = 0.
         times = cputim()
         do 20 j = 1,ncycle
           do 10 i = 1,maxnpt
             b(i) = a(i)*a(i)
      10   continue
           sum = sum + b(maxnpt)
      20 continue
         times = cputim() - times
         b(maxnpt) = b(maxnpt) + sum
         return
         end

(By the way, the reason for throwing in the variable  sum  is in case the
compiler is smart enough to drop the  do 20  loop since this simply repeats
the  do 10  loop  ncycle  times.)

Ed Overman



